 iff-flowers blossomed in the fertile soil of the Atlanta comedy scene.\n\nS
 ince moving to Texas in 2021\, The Crab Man went from living in his Ford Es
 cape to winning the inaugural Austin Comedy Competition. After his stinky l
 ittle victory\, Daft Rocket (as no one calls him) successfully auditioned t
 o join the first class of Door Guys at Joe Rogan’s Comedy Mothership\, wh
 ere he performed alongside some of the biggest names in comedy. In early 20
 24\, Rocket was named as the newest regular on Kill Tony.\n\nOver the eons\
 , Daft Rocket has brought his unique brand of drug-fueled nonsense comedy t
 o SXSW\, Skankfest Vegas\, the Boston Comedy Festival\, Aloha Comedy Festiv
 al\, and many more.\n\nCouples Package includes:\n\n- 2 premium seats\n- $9
